1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,782
An inbound call center answers the customers who call you.

2
00:00:04,782 --> 00:00:07,205
This video follows the whole story:

3
00:00:07,205 --> 00:00:12,227
the features to turn on, the order to set things up, and what each person does.

4
00:00:12,227 --> 00:00:17,250
Calls never connect on this demo site, so the live parts are shown with slides.

5
00:00:21,850 --> 00:00:25,935
This is for managers and administrators who set up a phone line for

6
00:00:25,935 --> 00:00:29,460
customers, and for the supervisors and agents who run it.

7
00:00:30,210 --> 00:00:34,246
A customer who calls your number hears a welcome and, if you want

8
00:00:34,246 --> 00:00:35,667
one, a keypad menu.

9
00:00:35,667 --> 00:00:39,703
The call waits in the right queue, with hold music and updates on

10
00:00:39,703 --> 00:00:44,250
their place in line, and is offered to a free agent with the right skills.

11
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:50,645
After hours, callers hear a closed message, and are held, sent to voicemail,

12
00:00:50,645 --> 00:00:54,500
moved to another queue, or refused, as you choose.

13
00:00:55,250 --> 00:00:59,440
Agents answer in the soft phone and record the outcome.

14
00:00:59,440 --> 00:01:04,180
Supervisors watch the queues live, listen in, and read reports.

15
00:01:08,368 --> 00:01:12,630
Your administrator turns on the features in Tools, Features.

16
00:01:12,630 --> 00:01:15,536
Telephony and your provider come first.

17
00:01:15,536 --> 00:01:21,735
Then Contact Center Work Distribution for queues, Inbound Entry Points, and Inbound Voice.

18
00:01:21,735 --> 00:01:27,998
Agents need Contact Center Agents, and supervisors need Supervision and the Live Dashboard.

19
00:01:29,598 --> 00:01:34,600
Contact Center Agent Entitlements is recommended once you have more than one team.

20
00:01:34,600 --> 00:01:39,488
A phone provider account, with the numbers customers will call, comes first, and

21
00:01:39,488 --> 00:01:43,694
the Agent role needs the permission to use the telephony soft phone.

22
00:01:43,694 --> 00:01:46,138
Supervisors have the Supervisor role.

23
00:01:50,338 --> 00:01:52,376
Start with what customers dial.

24
00:01:52,376 --> 00:01:56,892
List your numbers, set your opening hours, and upload hold music and prompts

25
00:01:56,892 --> 00:01:58,158
if you want them.

26
00:01:58,908 --> 00:02:00,927
Then the places calls wait.

27
00:02:00,927 --> 00:02:04,718
Create a queue for each team, such as Sales and Support.

28
00:02:05,468 --> 00:02:06,942
Then the people.

29
00:02:06,942 --> 00:02:12,568
Decide who works each queue with agent entitlements, skills and break reasons.

30
00:02:13,318 --> 00:02:15,035
Then route the number.

31
00:02:15,035 --> 00:02:19,511
An entry point sends the number to a queue, with a welcome message,

32
00:02:19,511 --> 00:02:21,718
a closed action and voicemail.

33
00:02:22,468 --> 00:02:27,968
Last, the house rules, the phone apps, and training for agents and supervisors.

34
00:02:32,141 --> 00:02:37,349
Add each number customers call under Omnichannel Addresses, with Voice calls ticked.

35
00:02:37,349 --> 00:02:40,301
These are the numbers the entry points route.

36
00:02:40,770 --> 00:02:45,580
Create a business hours calendar with your weekly hours and holidays.

37
00:02:45,580 --> 00:02:50,391
A queue or an entry point that uses it is closed outside those hours.

38
00:02:50,391 --> 00:02:53,470
A disabled calendar never closes anything.

39
00:02:57,677 --> 00:03:00,607
Create a queue for each team under Queues.

40
00:03:00,607 --> 00:03:02,804
Give it a Name, such as Sales.

41
00:03:02,804 --> 00:03:07,137
The routing strategy decides which free agent gets the next call.

42
00:03:09,970 --> 00:03:15,790
The business hours calendar and the after-hours action say what happens outside opening hours.

43
00:03:15,790 --> 00:03:19,690
The service level threshold is how long a caller should wait.

44
00:03:24,029 --> 00:03:28,205
The overflow queue takes callers after a wait, and the hold music, the

45
00:03:28,205 --> 00:03:32,546
announcements and the callback key set what callers hear while they wait.

46
00:03:32,546 --> 00:03:33,699
Save the queue.

47
00:03:37,918 --> 00:03:41,752
Add a Voice calls entry point under Inbound entry points.

48
00:03:41,752 --> 00:03:44,978
Give it a Name, and pick the number it answers.

49
00:03:44,978 --> 00:03:49,298
A number is answered by one enabled entry point for each channel.

50
00:03:51,082 --> 00:03:53,835
Set Route to a queue, and pick Sales.

51
00:03:53,835 --> 00:03:59,022
Pick the business hours calendar, and the closed action, such as voicemail.

52
00:04:04,274 --> 00:04:08,589
Write the welcome message callers hear, and the closed message.

53
00:04:08,589 --> 00:04:10,715
Choose where voicemail goes.

54
00:04:10,715 --> 00:04:16,406
A keypad menu can be built in the same form, when callers should choose a department.

55
00:04:16,406 --> 00:04:17,094
Save.

56
00:04:21,323 --> 00:04:25,200
Give each agent their queues under Agent entitlements.

57
00:04:25,200 --> 00:04:29,853
Open the entitlement of an agent, and add Sales to Allowed queues.

58
00:04:29,853 --> 00:04:34,764
The queue's priority and delay say how the agent backs up other teams.

59
00:04:34,764 --> 00:04:38,383
Skills decide who can take work that requires one.

60
00:04:38,843 --> 00:04:43,329
Supervisors see only the queues on their own entitlement record.

61
00:04:43,329 --> 00:04:47,623
An empty live dashboard almost always means a missing record.

62
00:04:51,823 --> 00:04:56,135
Each agent installs the phone app, signs in to their queues from the

63
00:04:56,135 --> 00:05:01,613
Work tab of the soft phone, sets themselves Available, and records a voicemail greeting.

64
00:05:02,363 --> 00:05:06,849
When a call arrives, the agent's bar shows the offer with a countdown.

65
00:05:06,849 --> 00:05:11,689
The agent accepts, talks, hangs up, and lands in Wrap-up until they complete

66
00:05:11,689 --> 00:05:13,933
the activity with a disposition.

67
00:05:14,683 --> 00:05:19,249
A supervisor sees the call on the live dashboard, while it waits and

68
00:05:19,249 --> 00:05:25,173
while it is connected, and can listen, whisper or barge in, and work the shared voicemail.

69
00:05:25,923 --> 00:05:31,343
Call insights, Queue usage and Agent productivity show how the line performs.

70
00:05:35,543 --> 00:05:40,156
To check that it works, have an agent sign in to the queue and be Available.

71
00:05:40,156 --> 00:05:44,713
Call the number from another phone during opening hours, and listen for the

72
00:05:44,713 --> 00:05:46,683
welcome message and the menu.

73
00:05:47,433 --> 00:05:52,843
Call again with no agent available, to hear the hold music and the announcements.

74
00:05:52,843 --> 00:05:57,943
Call outside opening hours to hear the closed message and the closed action.

75
00:05:58,693 --> 00:06:01,748
Start with one queue and one entry point.

76
00:06:01,748 --> 00:06:04,998
Test them, and add menus and overflow after.

77
00:06:04,998 --> 00:06:09,353
Clone a queue or an entry point from its Actions menu to make

78
00:06:09,353 --> 00:06:11,173
a similar one quickly.

79
00:06:11,923 --> 00:06:15,759
Callbacks need the Contact Center Outbound Dialer feature.

80
00:06:15,759 --> 00:06:19,715
To let an AI answer the line instead, see the use case about

81
00:06:19,715 --> 00:06:22,293
letting the AI answer your customers.

82
00:06:24,293 --> 00:06:29,896
List the numbers, open the queues, route each number, and give your agents their queues.

83
00:06:29,896 --> 00:06:34,843
Customers who call reach the right person, and supervisors can watch it live.

84
00:06:34,843 --> 00:06:36,393
Thanks for watching.

